Mill Plug-In SDK

A Plug-In adds URL schemes (protocols) or file formats to Mill. It is a
code resource of type 'MPlg', ID 128, with its entry point at byte 0, in
a file of type 'MPlg' and creator 'MiLL'. Put the file in the "Mill
Plug-Ins" folder next to Mill; mill://plugins lists what Mill found.
A font file (type 'FFIL') there may hold one too, to draw its families
from outlines (see Fonts in MillPlugIn.h).

Interface
  Every Plug-In file also has an 'MIfc' resource, ID 128: 2 bytes, the
  interface it was built for (kMillInterface, in MillInterface.h).
  Interfaces:MillPlugIn.r makes it, and Finger's MPW make file adds it
  (for CodeWarrior, see its Read Me). Mill reads it before it loads any
  code and skips a Plug-In without it or with another number. When a
  new Mill changes the interface, build again with its kit.

Folders
  Interfaces    MillPlugIn.h: the interface, with notes on every call;
                MillPlugIn.r: the 'MIfc' resource
  Glue          MillGlue.c: the entry point; add it to every Plug-In
  Examples      Finger: a small protocol Plug-In
  MPW           Finger.make, for MPW 3.4 (SC and Link)
  CodeWarrior   Finger's project, for CodeWarrior (CW4 and later)
